  "term": "magnetoencephalography",
  "definition": "Magnetoencephalography is a method for recording the magnetic fields produced by electrical activity in the brain from measurements taken over the head. It helps show where brain activity is occurring and can be used on its own or alongside electroencephalography for spontaneous or evoked brain activity.",
